# Day 02 — ArcGIS Pro Interface & Introduction

**Date:** 07.07.2026  
**Week:** 01 — GIS & ArcGIS Pro Foundations

## Overview

Day 02 focused on the ArcGIS Pro user interface, the introduction to ArcGIS Pro, and the first guided exercises for working with projects and geospatial data.

The day also covered the organization of the training environment, access to ArcGIS Pro, licensing, and the available learning resources.

## Topics Covered

### 1. Training Organization & Resources

- Review of the course overview and daily training structure
- Access to the ArcGIS Pro handbook
- Organization of course materials and training resources
- Use of the Alfatraining remote PC environment
- ArcGIS Pro configuration and settings

The daily and weekly training schedules were introduced as a reference for following the course and reviewing missed content.

### 2. ArcGIS Pro User Interface

The ArcGIS Pro interface was introduced using the official ArcGIS Pro handbook as a reference.

Key topics included:

- ArcGIS Pro user interface
- Application structure
- Main interface components
- Navigation within ArcGIS Pro
- Working environment for GIS projects

**Reference:** ArcGIS Pro Handbook, Chapter 4, Sections 4.1 and 4.2

### 3. Introduction to ArcGIS Pro

The first practical exercises introduced the basic concepts and workflow of ArcGIS Pro.

The exercises focused on:

- Introducing ArcGIS Pro
- Understanding the ArcGIS Pro working environment
- Navigating and exploring geospatial data
- Getting familiar with the basic project workflow

### 4. Quick-Start Tutorials

Additional ArcGIS Pro quick-start tutorials were used to reinforce the introductory concepts.

The exercises included:

- Creating an ArcGIS Pro project
- Introducing ArcGIS Pro
- Navigating geospatial data

